":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"S3/ADLS","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bronze, Silver storage layers","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Airflow","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Scheduling, orchestration, retry logic","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Snowflake","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Gold layer warehouse for BI","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Parquet","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Efficient storage format for Silver","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"IAM","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Permissions for S3, Snowflake access","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"ETL/ELT","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"ELT pattern — load raw to Bronze, transform in place","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Medallion","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bronze/Silver/Gold architecture","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"1d36762e-e1e5-44da-b4f7-fd1e05878b43","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"This pipeline touches every major topic you''ve studied. Understanding this flow end-to-end makes you interview-ready.","type":"text"}],"id":"48a27f14-2f27-4614-b931-0d3c976b365f","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"id":"50d4df06-8e6f-41c4-9363-01a11298e113","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"9. Interview-Level Understanding","type":"text"}],"id":"13198964-45cd-4c1e-94c8-1369e0d9af4b","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":2,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Interview Question 1:","type":"text"}],"id":"0f1e4a3e-127f-44d3-b72a-89706d64abdf","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"\"Walk me through how you would build a pipeline to ingest daily sales data from an API into a reporting table.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"a2213b40-1df0-46b5-8415-44f4d95ce3e1","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Strong Answer:","type":"text"}],"id":"1d0e72c4-c934-4ee0-9e1b-658940b8d384","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"I would design a multi-stage ELT pipeline using the Medallion Architecture — Bronze, Silver, Gold — orchestrated by Airflow and processing data with Spark and SQL.","type":"text"}],"id":"cc68a4f2-5512-4add-980b-00ef022f95cd","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"First, I''d use a ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Python script","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" to extract data from the sales API. This script would run daily at 1 AM, triggered by Airflow. It would call the API with the execution date, handle authentication, and write the raw JSON response to the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Bronze layer","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" in S3, partitioned by date — like ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"s3://bucket/bronze/sales/date=2025-07-15/","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":". This preserves the raw data exactly as received for auditability and reprocessing.","type":"text"}],"id":"e5c9967a-89e8-4219-85e2-57f6dc6f1901","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Next, a ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Spark job","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" would read the Bronze JSON, apply ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"cleaning and validation","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — filter out rows with null order IDs, cast data types like converting date strings to proper DATE types, calculate derived fields like total revenue, and remove duplicates based on order ID. This cleaned data would be written to the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Silver layer","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" as Parquet files, again partitioned by date. Parquet is columnar and compressed, making it efficient for analytical queries.","type":"text"}],"id":"db6845b4-3e1e-4241-bcd0-8f14891eb91d","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Then, a ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"SQL aggregation","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — either in Spark SQL or directly in Snowflake — would read Silver data and calculate business KPIs like total revenue by region and product category, grouped by date. This aggregated data would be loaded into the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Gold layer","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — a Snowflake table that serves as the source for dashboards. The load would use a delete-then-insert pattern for the specific date to ensure idempotency.","type":"text"}],"id":"a3b48341-aeaf-400e-881f-2665e14b754d","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Finally, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Tableau or Power BI","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" would query the Gold table in Snowflake to visualize the data for business users.","type":"text"}],"id":"e2354c52-03e0-4d61-b86f-7e7001594120","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"The entire pipeline would be orchestrated by ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Airflow","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", which schedules the daily run, enforces task dependencies — extraction before cleaning, cleaning before aggregation — retries failed tasks automatically, and sends alerts if something breaks.","type":"text"}],"id":"17c8d761-9135-450f-977c-d89cfcdad760","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"For ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"failure recovery","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", if the Spark cleaning job failed, I could rerun just that task because Bronze data is immutable. The pipeline is designed to be ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"idempotent","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — rerunning for the same date produces the same result with no duplicates, because Silver and Gold use overwrite or delete-insert patterns.","type":"text"}],"id":"d2eb73b7-1945-4046-aec9-55bdabc6ea11","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"This design separates concerns, scales with data growth, and provides full end-to-end visibility from source to dashboard.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"cba525a1-be32-4ebb-8846-886f2bce614e","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"id":"75126e66-1db2-41a8-8c1e-e0bfa9568a97","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Interview Question 2:","type":"text"}],"id":"22ab8ace-aa98-4ea1-9ac5-ccbf80d35947","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"\"What would you do if the pipeline fails halfway?\"","type":"text"}],"id":"8f7307a9-3ea5-40d5-a530-3d525d953778","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Strong Answer:","type":"text"}],"id":"0a791ba8-f288-4d30-87db-d7bf8fac5a49","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"The first step is to ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"identify where the failure occurred","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" using the orchestration tool''s UI — in Airflow, I''d check the Web UI to see which task failed, then view the logs for that specific task to understand the root cause.","type":"text"}],"id":"3f820592-856b-46aa-b7a0-654777d60621","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Once I know the failure point — say, the Spark cleaning job failed due to out-of-memory errors — I''d ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"fix the underlying issue","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":". In this case, I''d increase the Spark executor memory in the job configuration or optimize the transformation logic to reduce memory usage.","type":"text"}],"id":"24faecf1-3030-4a6c-8996-ab430952ad7e","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Then I''d ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"rerun just the failed task","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" from the Airflow UI. Because the pipeline is designed with ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"idempotency","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" in mind, rerunning a task for a specific date safely overwrites the output for that date without duplicating data or affecting other dates. For example, the Spark job writes to Silver using ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"mode(\"overwrite\").partitionBy(\"date\")","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", so rerunning for ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"date=2025-07-15","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" replaces only that partition.","type":"text"}],"id":"31e729d7-124d-43fb-9d8d-d47b8ec0c4a8","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Airflow''s ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"dependency management","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" ensures that once the failed task succeeds, downstream tasks automatically run. So if the cleaning task was blocking the aggregation task, Airflow will immediately run aggregation once cleaning completes.","type":"text"}],"id":"9151f986-4a04-470d-86dc-5185a9f91b77","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Importantly, I wouldn''t need to re-extract from the source API because the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"Bronze layer is immutable","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — the raw data is still there. This is why preserving raw data in Bronze is critical for failure recovery.","type":"text"}],"id":"0db3014c-b3ff-49dd-9c4a-c4cef9cd402d","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Finally, I''d investigate whether this was a one-time issue or a systemic problem. If it''s systemic — like data volume growing beyond current capacity — I''d proactively adjust the pipeline configuration or refactor the logic to prevent future failures.","type":"text"}],"id":"2fb9ebee-e54e-42d5-b6e7-b160e29b030b","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"This approach — identify, fix, rerun, monitor — is the standard practice for production data pipeline failure recovery.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"99a5a812-f035-4cd1-a249-ee4fa59684fd","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"id":"a6b98234-6103-4b2c-8b58-659749873cb6","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Interview Question 3:","type":"text"}],"id":"dca24353-8b6b-4da6-8c96-5d1ea1ae2739","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"\"What is the difference between full load and incremental load?\"","type":"text"}],"id":"e03c74ff-3e56-4e18-9440-e40ac84fa142","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Strong Answer:","type":"text"}],"id":"13bdd2aa-15e8-4c7d-af4d-9c2d0112f53c","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"Full load and incremental load are two different strategies for extracting data from a source system, and the choice between them depends on data volume, performance requirements, and whether historical data changes.","type":"text"}],"id":"5c531aee-dc45-4e5f-9cec-e30363ba9755","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"full load","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" extracts all data from the source every time the pipeline runs, regardless of what has changed. For example, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"SELECT * FROM orders","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — every order, every day. The advantage is simplicity — you don''t need to track state or worry about missing records. The disadvantage is cost and performance — if you have 10 million historical orders and only 10,000 new orders daily, you''re reprocessing 99.9% of the same data every day, wasting compute and time.","type":"text"}],"id":"06a37d0a-4941-4cae-84ec-985fa13a24f4","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"incremental load","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" extracts only new or changed data since the last successful pipeline run. For example, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE updated_at > last_watermark","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":". This is far more efficient because you process only the delta, not the entire dataset. The trade-off is complexity — you need to maintain a watermark — a timestamp or ID that tracks what was last processed — and you need to handle edge cases like late-arriving data or updates to old records.","type":"text"}],"id":"3d74eabc-300a-4414-a86b-dceb3b1c7d21","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"In practice, I''d use ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"full load","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" for small, relatively static datasets where simplicity is more important than efficiency — say, a lookup table with a few thousand reference codes. I''d use ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"incremental load","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" for large, growing transactional datasets like orders, logs, or events, where data volume makes full load impractical.","type":"text"}],"id":"caafdbe0-882d-4051-a5be-0365d150b44f","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"The watermark is typically stored in a metadata table or Airflow variable and only updated after the pipeline successfully completes. This ensures that if the pipeline fails, the next run picks up from the last successful state without missing data.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"06442a2a-536e-40a9-841f-f01f73b6c083","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"id":"d9b783cd-0b19-4cc6-89f1-da5e0057f590","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Interview Question 4:","type":"text"}],"id":"8ef62bd7-c640-4d79-a7bc-adc548486b18","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"\"Why is idempotency important in data pipelines?\"","type":"text"}],"id":"6d4de3c5-6c1e-4749-8db2-9dfb17723a06","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Strong Answer:","type":"text"}],"id":"1714e6fd-8525-457c-8173-f80318630f36","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"Idempotency is critical because pipelines ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"will be rerun","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — not as an exception, but as a routine part of production operations — and reruns must be safe.","type":"text"}],"id":"1e111dfe-f1fc-4ed9-b7f4-fe2b389e6ea3","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Pipelines get rerun for many reasons: a task fails due to a transient error like a network timeout, a bug is discovered in transformation logic and historical data needs to be reprocessed, late-arriving data requires reprocessing yesterday''s partition, or a scheduled retry is triggered by the orchestration tool.","type":"text"}],"id":"24fc9c2b-666f-492a-982a-509c6f9bff26","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Without idempotency, rerunning a pipeline can cause serious problems. If the pipeline appends data instead of overwriting, you get ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"duplicates","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — revenue is double-counted, metrics are wrong, and business decisions are based on corrupted data. If transformations have side effects — like incrementing counters or sending emails — rerunning triggers those side effects again.","type":"text"}],"id":"0fe09dda-f3bb-4e7a-87fd-fb225c44f97c","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Idempotent design ensures that running the pipeline multiple times for the same input produces the same output. For example, writing to Silver using ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"mode(\"overwrite\").partitionBy(\"date\")","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" means rerunning for ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"date=2025-07-15","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" replaces that partition with fresh data — no duplicates. Or using a delete-then-insert pattern in SQL ensures exactly one set of records for each date.","type":"text"}],"id":"0a8ec5c3-3724-4160-8231-f28a55361005","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Idempotency gives confidence that failures are recoverable. When a pipeline fails at 2 AM, the on-call engineer doesn''t need to manually clean up partial data or worry about cascading corruption. They just fix the issue, rerun the pipeline, and trust that the result is correct. This is essential for production reliability.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"aa4f75e0-7c6f-4ac3-b3c3-c8a43e82fdd7","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"id":"42f7eb96-906c-4ac7-a12d-9682676af67c","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Interview Question 5:","type":"text"}],"id":"11e48c70-9d1b-4422-b93c-0f7a34548c7a","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"\"Where would you add data quality checks?\"","type":"text"}],"id":"8f93f659-c9fa-4011-91c1-075b524e9749","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Strong Answer:","type":"text"}],"id":"360b9aba-6d82-4355-bfc3-91013ba83ae0","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"I''d add data quality checks at multiple stages throughout the pipeline, with each stage validating what matters at that point.","type":"text"}],"id":"3767a8ad-365a-42b4-84e1-2ecdca2b5899","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"First, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"at extraction","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", I''d validate the API response — check for HTTP 200 status, confirm the response is valid JSON, and log the number of records extracted. This ensures we''re getting data from the source at all.","type":"text"}],"id":"607f91e3-3bd9-43d9-9611-ec84aca01463","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Second, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"at Bronze ingestion","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", I''d verify that the expected number of files or records landed in S3, and check that the file is not corrupted. This is usually a simple count and file size check.","type":"text"}],"id":"f621e007-be6f-4575-a637-0b8b1338196f","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Third, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"during Bronze to Silver transformation","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", I''d enforce ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"schema validation","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — check that all expected columns are present and have the correct data types. I''d also apply ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"null checks","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" on critical fields like order ID and customer ID, filtering out or quarantining invalid records rather than letting them propagate. I''d check for and remove duplicates based on primary keys. And I''d validate business rules — like ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"quantity > 0","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"amount >= 0","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":".","type":"text"}],"id":"6b3e6e59-4b93-4a0c-9cde-43256b2f7fc0","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Fourth, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"after Silver is written","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", I''d perform ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"reconciliation checks","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" — compare the row count in Silver to Bronze to ensure no data was lost during cleaning. If more than a threshold percentage of records is filtered out — say, 10% — the pipeline should alert or fail because that suggests a data quality issue at the source.","type":"text"}],"id":"9a084b83-787c-43fa-ad9e-3682baad1cf0","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Fifth, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"during Silver to Gold aggregation","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", I''d validate that aggregated totals make sense. For example, total revenue in Gold should not exceed total revenue in Silver. I''d also check for unexpected nulls in aggregated columns.","type":"text"}],"id":"6cf88648-cfa4-4d1b-a16c-01e679a48847","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Finally, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true,"italic":true},"text":"at consumption","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":", business users perform manual spot checks on dashboards — if numbers look wrong, they report it, and we trace back through the pipeline to find the issue.","type":"text"}],"id":"2611549a-d262-40bf-aedb-8c49c196b950","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"Each check should log results and, if critical checks fail, the pipeline should stop and alert the team rather than silently propagating bad data downstream. This layered approach ensures data quality is validated at each transformation boundary.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"447c506c-8637-46b6-8488-2ef320f02097","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"id":"5ab9bcd6-41b9-4673-8dfd-786f30195fde","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"10. C.A.C.O. Application","type":"text"}],"id":"db7e3b6d-942e-46ea-831e-f61f1e4bcc5a","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":2,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Concept","type":"text"}],"id":"cdccfef9-91d1-48be-b5b5-52962bf47b10","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"end-to-end data pipeline","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" moves data from source systems through multiple transformation stages to final consumption. It follows the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Medallion Architecture","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" (Bronze → Silver → Gold), uses ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"ELT","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" (load raw, transform in place), employs ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"incremental loading","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" for efficiency, ensures ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"idempotency","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" for safe reruns, validates ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"data quality","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" at each stage, and is ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"orchestrated","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" by tools like Airflow. Understanding the full flow — not just one tool — is the foundation of data engineering.","type":"text"}],"id":"3f081c9b-689c-4fce-b17f-4419ec315a32","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"id":"89eff258-e34f-42a9-af5c-b19ff164dd05","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Architecture","type":"text"}],"id":"fe212f67-e91e-46d3-8239-344db6ae9bb7","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Source System (API, Database, Event Stream)\n    ↓ Extract (Python, JDBC)\nBronze Layer (S3/ADLS — raw data, immutable)\n    ↓ Transform (Spark, dbt)\nSilver Layer (S3/ADLS — clean, validated)\n    ↓ Aggregate (Spark SQL, Snowflake SQL)\nGold Layer (Warehouse — business-ready KPIs)\n    ↓ Consume (BI tools, ML models, analysts)\n\nOrchestrated by: Airflow\nMonitored by: Logging, Airflow UI, alerts\nSecured by: IAM roles, least privilege","type":"text"}],"id":"ab02d4bb-86de-42fb-9570-2016305c01ba","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"id":"5dc66b09-baaa-4761-b2fa-1fca1e88a8cb","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Code — Simple Pseudocode Pipeline Flow","type":"text"}],"id":"a7744d07-c765-4c8c-9105-1122354a5275","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# STAGE 1: Extract API Data\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndef extract_sales_data(date):\n    response = api.get(f\"/sales?date={date}\")\n    raw_data = response.json()\n    write_to_s3(f\"bronze/sales/date={date}/\", raw_data)\n    return len(raw_data)\n\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# STAGE 2: Clean and Validate → Silver\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndef clean_to_silver(date):\n    df = spark.read.json(f\"s3://bucket/bronze/sales/date={date}/\")\n    \n    # Clean\n    clean_df = df.filter(\"order_id IS NOT NULL\") \\\n                 .dropDuplicates([\"order_id\"]) \\\n                 .withColumn(\"amount\", col(\"amount\").cast(\"decimal\"))\n    \n    # Validate\n    if clean_df.count() == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"No valid records\")\n    \n    # Write\n    clean_df.write.mode(\"overwrite\") \\\n                  .partitionBy(\"date\") \\\n                  .parquet(f\"s3://bucket/silver/sales/\")\n    \n    return clean_df.count()\n\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# STAGE 3: Aggregate → Gold\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndef aggregate_to_gold(date):\n    # Delete existing data for date\n    sql_delete = f\"DELETE FROM gold.sales WHERE date = ''{date}''\"\n    execute_sql(sql_delete)\n    \n    # Insert aggregated data\n    sql_insert = f\"\"\"\n    INSERT INTO gold.sales\n    SELECT date, region, SUM(amount) AS revenue\n    FROM silver.sales\n    WHERE date = ''{date}''\n    GROUP BY date, region\n    \"\"\"\n    execute_sql(sql_insert)\n    \n    return \"Success\"\n\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ORCHESTRATION: Airflow DAG\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nwith DAG(''sales_pipeline'', schedule_interval=''@daily'') as dag:\n    \n    task_extract = PythonOperator(\n        task_id=''extract'',\n        python_callable=extract_sales_data\n    )\n    \n    task_clean = PythonOperator(\n        task_id=''clean_to_silver'',\n        python_callable=clean_to_silver\n    )\n    \n    task_aggregate = PythonOperator(\n        task_id=''aggregate_to_gold'',\n        python_callable=aggregate_to_gold\n    )\n    \n    # Dependencies\n    task_extract >> task_clean >> task_aggregate","type":"text"}],"id":"5756d713-8e1e-4dce-8147-e5ddcb709482","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"id":"caca48d8-b869-43f5-bd8b-732a9282d114","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Optimization / Interview Tactics","type":"text"}],"id":"79111c36-2a71-459a-a354-88af2a60eb87","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Lead with the water purification mental model","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — makes pipelines relatable to anyone","type":"text"}],"id":"65d74e2b-adb0-44f6-bae1-301f8efe83c9","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Always mention Medallion Architecture (Bronze/Silver/Gold)","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — shows modern data engineering awareness","type":"text"}],"id":"dfa4823d-3d4f-4fb9-b5dc-a4a9277d9ba5","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Emphasize idempotency","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — this is a differentiator at junior level; most juniors don''t think about it","type":"text"}],"id":"3496b6fe-2114-4186-943d-cd1490d1e9d8","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Connect every tool to the pipeline stage","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — \"Airflow orchestrates, Spark transforms, S3 stores, Snowflake serves\"","type":"text"}],"id":"8e028375-9890-48be-84e5-f577399e3547","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Use realistic examples","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — sales data, customer data, event logs — not abstract \"data\"","type":"text"}],"id":"3c4b5aac-2503-44ac-b4da-cccb30673ef4","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Mention failure recovery explicitly","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — shows you think about production reliability","type":"text"}],"id":"281239ba-7ef9-420e-9904-bbf2b07fd6e6","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Know the difference between full and incremental load","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — common interview question","type":"text"}],"id":"385f97fc-c422-48d6-a009-adb205a11e48","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Orchestration: Airflow, Prefect, Dagster","type":"text"}],"id":"12291515-09c5-471d-b3d2-62709b6235f8","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Transformation: Spark, dbt, SQL","type":"text"}],"id":"2f6cfe76-00f2-46e9-a362-b2037ead9963","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Storage: S3, ADLS, GCS","type":"text"}],"id":"19cb711b-b1b4-489f-8ab3-40dcd8067396","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Warehouse: Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift","type":"text"}],"id":"82ce4191-8b1d-44c1-a241-736d082e8105","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"BI: Tableau, Power BI, Looker","type":"text"}],"id":"09135648-2f4d-488f-809b-fab197c18e85","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"}],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Name real tools correctly:","type":"text"}],"id":"1acc85fc-26c0-4330-a929-998194c5b2b1","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"For Sysco LABS / EY GDS / Dialog Axiata:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" These companies run production pipelines at scale — emphasize reliability, monitoring, and cost efficiency","type":"text"}],"id":"699ec169-3c91-4176-9f2a-d3be348ec03a","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"id":"1c68654b-73cc-4323-aa66-1efe2c4309da","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"11. Final Interview Summary","type":"text"}],"id":"04edab80-6891-405f-8388-5c4019526ead","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":2,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Key Terms","type":"text"}],"id":"125863d4-58bf-494d-994b-932b5ca64cb3","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":{"columnWidths":[null,null],"headerRows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Term","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Definition","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Data Pipeline","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Automated workflow moving data from source to destination with transformations","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Source System","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Where data originates (API, database, event stream)","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Extraction","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Reading data from source systems","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Loading","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Writing data to a destination (S3, warehouse)","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Transformation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Changing data structure, format, or content","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Bronze Layer","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Raw, immutable data exactly as received","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Silver Layer","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Cleaned, validated, trusted data","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Gold Layer","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Aggregated, business-ready KPIs","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Full Load","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Extract all data every time","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Incremental Load","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Extract only new/changed data since last run","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Watermark","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Marker tracking what was last successfully processed","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Idempotency","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Running pipeline multiple times produces same result — no duplicates","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Data Validation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Checks ensuring data quality (schema, nulls, ranges)","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Aggregation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Summarizing data (SUM, COUNT, AVG by group)","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Orchestration","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Scheduling and coordinating pipeline tasks (Airflow)","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Failure Recovery","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Ability to safely rerun after failures","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Reprocessing","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Re-running pipeline for historical dates","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"bd5b90aa-ac80-48d9-8ad8-f1cbaf2c7daa","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"id":"41c9322f-334c-4334-bae6-610d60b62a81","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Must-Remember Points","type":"text"}],"id":"01e28040-b309-42a4-896d-e4c32daefbaf","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"End-to-end pipeline flow:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Source → Bronze → Silver → Gold → Consumption","type":"text"}],"id":"47016e4e-143f-440a-a42f-f05cbdb12b39","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Bronze","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" = raw, immutable; ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Silver","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" = clean, validated; ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Gold","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" = aggregated, business-ready","type":"text"}],"id":"4bee4ed3-31c5-44c3-9c5e-000bdcdb0547","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"ELT pattern:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Load raw to Bronze, transform in place (not before loading)","type":"text"}],"id":"e6c2babe-ac7c-4acc-8b62-bd8bfc7ba469","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Full load","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" = simple but expensive; ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Incremental load","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" = efficient but complex","type":"text"}],"id":"8ab93e06-9280-4ee1-a526-da6c18191e66","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Watermark","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" tracks last successful extraction — critical for incremental load","type":"text"}],"id":"e6088587-2dd0-4e43-8e65-9abd42f04511","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Idempotency","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" = running pipeline multiple times produces same result — essential for production","type":"text"}],"id":"be24e023-3e02-4636-b601-c2479293dae1","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Failure recovery:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Rerun failed tasks; Bronze is the reprocessing safety net","type":"text"}],"id":"118a1028-554b-4331-b3a2-d9b1d5072a2a","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Data validation","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" happens at multiple stages — extraction, cleaning, aggregation","type":"text"}],"id":"e88c0a39-b1d2-4985-9474-0164447efec2","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Orchestration","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" (Airflow) schedules, monitors, retries, alerts","type":"text"}],"id":"c31ab74c-89a9-44db-833d-ab4400473e02","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Every stage uses different tools:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Python (extract), Spark (transform), SQL (aggregate), S3 (store), Snowflake (warehouse)","type":"text"}],"id":"855fc2cd-b133-44a8-8fbb-b2a1a69ee52c","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"✅ ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Think end-to-end, not just one tool","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" — this is what makes a data engineer valuable","type":"text"}],"id":"8d358984-32a1-480b-bc64-a21f972628c5","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"id":"880f8ab2-2a27-4ddb-b12c-726dd58c5c00","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"3 Interview-Ready One-Liners","type":"text"}],"id":"5d787028-747e-45d3-8b45-f1191bd60aa1","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"1.","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"An end-to-end data pipeline follows the Medallion Architecture — extracting raw data into the Bronze layer where it''s preserved exactly as received, transforming and validating it into the trusted Silver layer, aggregating it into business-ready KPIs in the Gold layer, and serving it to dashboards and analysts — with Airflow orchestrating the flow, Spark handling transformations at scale, and S3 or a cloud warehouse providing storage.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"76010d8a-56a1-4f46-b969-3c21439b49fc","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"2.","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"Idempotency is critical in production pipelines because pipelines will be rerun — whether due to failures, bug fixes, or late-arriving data — and rerunning must produce the same result without duplicates, which we achieve through patterns like overwriting specific date partitions, using delete-then-insert for target tables, and preserving raw data in Bronze as the immutable reprocessing safety net.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"92caf8e7-719e-4788-8f23-74eb262243a6","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"3.","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"\"The difference between full load and incremental load is that full load extracts all data every time regardless of what changed — simple but expensive — while incremental load uses a watermark to extract only new or changed records since the last successful run — efficient and scalable but requiring state management and careful handling of late-arriving data and updates.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"066f35ba-04d4-4066-8429-e1c35b626daa","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"id":"c963bee2-5e52-464f-91b4-d075a4d63272","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Common Mistakes to Avoid","type":"text"}],"id":"c46904c1-6a90-4ad3-bd31-c502712ce392","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":{"columnWidths":[null,null,null],"headerRows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Mistake","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Why It''s Wrong","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Correct Understanding","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Thinking pipelines are just ETL scripts","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Pipelines require orchestration, monitoring, failure handling, idempotency","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Pipelines are production systems with orchestration, validation, recovery","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Not preserving raw data in Bronze","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Loses ability to reprocess; debugging requires re-extraction","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Always preserve raw data — Bronze is the permanent record","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Designing non-idempotent pipelines","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Reruns cause duplicates and data corruption","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Every stage must be safely rerunnable — overwrite partitions, use upsert","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Using full load for everything","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Wastes compute and money at scale","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Use incremental load for large, growing datasets","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Not validating data quality","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bad data propagates to dashboards and breaks trust","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Validate at every boundary — extraction, cleaning, aggregation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Forgetting orchestration","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Manually running tasks doesn''t scale","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Always orchestrate with Airflow or equivalent","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Not thinking about failure scenarios","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Production pipelines fail — unprepared teams scramble","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Design for failure — logging, retries, alerts, idempotency","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Treating Silver as final destination","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Silver is intermediate; Gold serves business users","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Silver is the foundation; Gold is the serving layer","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"55918507-046b-450c-8110-8a63a2125883","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"id":"4f301e23-095a-431e-bf7d-8bd17e8192cc","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Remember the water purification system.","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Raw water from the source (API, database) flows into the collection tank (Bronze), passes through filtering and chemical treatment (Silver transformations), becomes safe drinking water (Gold KPIs), is stored in reservoirs (warehouse), and delivered to consumers (dashboards, analysts). The plant monitors every stage (Airflow), stops if quality checks fail (validation), and can reprocess batches safely (idempotency). This is exactly how a production data pipeline works. Master this mental model, and you can confidently explain any data engineering system end-to-end.","type":"text"}],"id":"eaf0c5a9-129d-4434-894b-444066e338e0","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quote"},{"children":[],"content":[],"id":"797e124e-0602-4f71-a285-c70b839b255b","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"}]'::jsonb, '3e9e3dd3-a59b-4b02-968a-ee95e7317583') ON CONFLICT ("node_id") DO UPDATE SET "bad_example" = EXCLUDED."bad_example", "completed_at" = EXCLUDED."completed_at", "created_at" = EXCLUDED."created_at", "definition" = EXCLUDED."definition", "good_example" = EXCLUDED."good_example", "is_completed" = EXCLUDED."is_completed", "key_points" = EXCLUDED."key_points", "last_edited" = EXCLUDED."last_edited", "map_id" = EXCLUDED."map_id", "mental_model" = EXCLUDED."mental_model", "notes" = EXCLUDED."notes", "resources" = EXCLUDED."resources", "rich_content" = EXCLUDED."rich_content", "user_id" = EXCLUDED."user_id";
