s at the Center","type":"text"}],"id":"1cbb916d-51c1-46fe-8d88-f111c6e8512e","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Because the fact table is the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"event recorder","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". Every dimension is a different lens through which you can view those events. The fact table references all lenses, making it the logical hub. Analysts join inward from the facts to the dimensions they care about for a given question.","type":"text"}],"id":"824c5b3f-d971-4c52-bd28-5e80bf7981cb","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"id":"fd6c7bd6-4e64-4682-995b-27021f60248f","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"5. Grain Understanding","type":"text"}],"id":"0faa15da-6d23-460f-a5aa-eb364389a571","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":2,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"What is Grain?","type":"text"}],"id":"51f52cd0-af11-412b-9a69-7aa578b5e76d","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Grain","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" is the precise definition of ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"what one single row in the fact table represents","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":".","type":"text"}],"id":"c83ededb-ed53-49ce-87b4-48100748366e","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"It is the most important design decision you make before writing a single column name.","type":"text"}],"id":"4fa1269d-f8ce-4b76-99b3-9aeccead7579","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Why Grain Must Be Defined First","type":"text"}],"id":"69ee282d-8909-40f6-89ff-db6c22049872","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"If you don''t define grain clearly:","type":"text"}],"id":"9f09c35c-1167-4732-b47b-ed3cc25c57c2","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"You won''t know which measures belong in the fact table","type":"text"}],"id":"7239736b-4f9b-4cdb-bb1a-f095c8075a74","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"You might mix events at different levels of detail","type":"text"}],"id":"218f65ab-f660-40d6-bc00-a5296b2faee9","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Queries will produce double-counting or incorrect aggregations","type":"text"}],"id":"f35c531f-e230-4adb-bab1-b8a839ca655f","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"The schema becomes unreliable for reporting","type":"text"}],"id":"f0846d71-6c9b-4334-b05d-385d195005eb","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"If you cannot state the grain in one clear sentence, the fact table design is incomplete.","type":"text"}],"id":"8f1ee524-c830-447e-b187-e97a5f05ea75","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default"},"type":"quo