r":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"household_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"store_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"basket_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"product_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"quantity","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"sales_value","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", discounts, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"week","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"transaction_timestamp","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", product metadata. citeturn30view0","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Excellent for revenue, discount, customer, and category analytics; strong grocery fit.","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Source Files is an educational/research sharing platform; check terms before redistributing raw files in your repo. citeturn24search1turn17view0","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Less natural for delivery and warehouse analytics; demographics are only available for part of the households. citeturn30view0","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Yes, but best for transaction, pricing, customer, and promotion sources rather than fulfillment-first sources.","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"DataCo Smart Supply Chain","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Mendeley official dataset page and Kaggle mirror. citeturn17view2turn29search3","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"A structured supply-chain dataset plus clickstream; public description mentions product types such as clothing, sports, and electronics, with variables like scheduled shipping days, actual shipping days, benefit per order, sales per customer, and delivery status. citeturn17view2turn29search3","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Delivery-status, shipping-schedule, order-benefit, and sales fields; one Kaggle mirror lists a 95.91 MB CSV. citeturn29search3","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Strong logistics and fulfillment analytics.","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Official Mendeley page lists CC BY 4.0. citeturn17view2","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Product domain is not foodservice, so Sysco relevance is weaker. citeturn17view2","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Yes, but the domain mismatch makes it less ideal as your flagship Sysco-targeted project.","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"1eebc29c-7ed3-4047-b287-b1c04828b98a","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Recommended default dataset:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Instacart Market Basket Analysis","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", with a ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"separate simulated price book","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"separate simulated fulfillment sources","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". That sounds counterintuitive at first, but it is actually a very defensible data engineering choice. The Instacart data gives you a strong food-category and order-line foundation, while the missing operational tables become an opportunity to model realistic source separation instead of pretending one public file has everything. Public Sysco context supports pricing, warehousing, delivery, and digital ordering as separate business concerns, so simulating them transparently is more credible than hiding them inside one monolithic transform. citeturn23search0turn27search18turn27search1turn1view0turn2view1turn10view0","type":"text"}],"id":"51057729-b98e-4eaf-9c75-fd39ca95d6d9","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"If you personally dislike synthetic pricing, the strongest alternative is ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"dunnhumby Complete Journey","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", because it already has transaction revenue and discount fields. The trade-off is that it is less naturally fulfillment-oriented. citeturn30view0turn17view0","type":"text"}],"id":"3099bdb7-f8cf-40f6-a79a-ddc5f1564983","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision I need to make:\nWhich dataset should I use?\n\nDataset options:\n1. Instacart Market Basket Analysis\n2. dunnhumby Complete Journey\n3. DataCo Smart Supply Chain\n\nRecommended dataset:\nInstacart Market Basket Analysis, plus a simulated price book and simulated warehouse/inventory/delivery sources\n\nWhy it is recommended:\nIt gives the strongest food-domain fit, a clean relational order/product structure, and a great foundation for source-system simulation.\n\nRisks or limitations:\nIt lacks explicit price, warehouse, supplier, and delivery-event data, so I must model those gaps honestly and deterministically.\n\nHow I can adapt it to a Sysco-inspired scenario:\nUse the public Instacart files as the order and product backbone, then create explicit simulated source tables for customer account profiles, price book, warehouses, inventory snapshots, and deliveries.\n\nInterview defense question:\nWhy did you choose this dataset and how did you adapt it?\n\nMy final choice:\n[leave blank for me]","type":"text"}],"id":"b9e94f0e-e4f1-466a-9660-62b00b89fde3","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Business Scenario and Architecture Choices","type":"text"}],"id":"cecff98c-d3a5-45cd-9722-8cbca6fbdafd","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":2,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Scenario versions","type":"text"}],"id":"64b70a26-ed28-44d4-8b2e-f5bd88babc41","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":{"columnWidths":[null,null,null,null,null],"headerRows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Scenario version","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Narrative","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Primary stakeholders","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Typical pain points","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Best questions it answers","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Distributor operations control tower","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"A foodservice distributor needs one reliable analytics layer that joins customer orders, order lines, product master, pricing, warehouse assignment, inventory health, and delivery performance.","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Operations manager, warehouse manager, logistics lead, supply chain analyst, sales manager","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Fragmented source systems, conflicting IDs, unclear fulfillment visibility, weak on-time and stock-risk reporting","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"What sold, who ordered it, where it was fulfilled, what was delayed, and where stock risk is rising","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Commercial growth and account analytics","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"The business wants customer, category, and order-behavior reporting to track growth, decline, and account concentration.","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Sales manager, finance analyst, customer success lead","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Slow reporting, unclear account trends, weak segment views","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Which categories and account segments are driving revenue and repeat behavior","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Inventory and replenishment watchlist","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"The business wants a daily view of stock risk, slow movers, and replenishment priorities across warehouses.","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Warehouse manager, procurement analyst, operations analyst","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Overstock, stockouts, poor prioritization, weak warehouse visibility","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Which SKUs need attention now and where inventory is imbalanced","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"d808f44c-402b-4566-8f09-c5151b43d361","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"My mentor recommendation is ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Distributor operations control tower","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". It is the best flagship story because it lets you speak about both business reporting and data-engineering mechanics. It also maps tightly to public Sysco themes: foodservice customers, daily delivery, inventory support, digital ordering, warehousing, and Sysco LABS’ data focus on orders and deliveries. citeturn1view0turn2view1turn0search11turn0search5turn8view1turn10view0","type":"text"}],"id":"9096e06a-95b6-45c6-9803-43de913a6aab","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision I need to make:\nWhich business scenario version should I commit to?\n\nOptions:\n1. Distributor operations control tower\n2. Commercial growth and account analytics\n3. Inventory and replenishment watchlist\n\nRecommended scenario:\nDistributor operations control tower\n\nWhy it is recommended:\nIt is broad enough to feel like real foodservice distribution, but still focused enough for a junior project if I keep version 1 disciplined.\n\nWhat makes it Sysco-relevant:\nIt reflects public Sysco themes: customer ordering, product distribution, warehouse operations, pricing, delivery, and operational reporting.\n\nInterview defense question:\nWhat real business problem does this project solve?\n\nMy final choice:\n[leave blank for me]","type":"text"}],"id":"396e9571-21d8-4de2-9b44-47b57b75e224","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Architecture options","type":"text"}],"id":"9e808792-66de-40ef-a370-ec95e84ed113","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":{"columnWidths":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"headerRows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Architecture option","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Difficulty","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Interview strength","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Build time","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Resume value","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Risk","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Best for","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Local production-minded stack using Python, Pandas, SQL, and PostgreSQL or DuckDB","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Low","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Medium","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Fast","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Medium","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Low","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"If your time is very tight and you want maximum simplicity","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Strong DE portfolio stack using Python, PySpark, Parquet, DuckDB or PostgreSQL, SQL, Power BI, custom validation, and a Makefile or CLI runner","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Medium","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"High","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Good","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"High","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Medium","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Best default flagship build","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Cloud-simulated stack using PySpark, Parquet, MinIO or S3-like storage, PostgreSQL or DuckDB, Docker, and optional Airflow","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Medium-high","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"High","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Slower","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"High if completed cleanly","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"High","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Only if you finish core scope early","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"bf411d59-b534-41d6-8299-45fedc9b1271","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Recommended architecture:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"the strong DE portfolio stack","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". Public Sysco LABS junior data-engineering material explicitly mentions Python, SQL, Spark, ETL/ELT, AWS-style data services, data warehousing, CI/CD, and large-volume data processing. A local PySpark-plus-Parquet design lets you demonstrate the same engineering ideas without spending your project on cloud setup. It also transfers well to EY GDS-style interviews, where public roles similarly emphasize SQL, Python, ETL/ELT, orchestration, cloud services, and modern data architectures. citeturn10view0turn13search1turn13search6turn13search7turn13search11","type":"text"}],"id":"cb6d35df-4d0e-46cc-877e-95e7d7934472","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision I need to make:\nWhich architecture should I build?\n\nOptions:\n1. Local production-minded stack\n2. Strong data engineering portfolio stack\n3. Cloud-simulated portfolio stack\n\nRecommended architecture:\nStrong data engineering portfolio stack\n\nWhy it is recommended:\nIt gives me Spark, Parquet, layered storage, SQL modeling, validation, and BI without overwhelming the project with infrastructure.\n\nWhat I must understand before choosing:\nI need to be able to explain why each layer exists, how reruns work, and why I did not deploy unnecessary tooling.\n\nRisk if I over-engineer:\nI may lose time on environment setup, orchestration, and containers and end up with a weaker business story, thinner SQL, and weaker documentation.\n\nInterview defense question:\nWhy did you choose this architecture?\n\nMy final choice:\n[leave blank for me]","type":"text"}],"id":"d05b3b84-a2f2-40b5-a211-90f60005f57f","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Architecture template and layer-by-layer guide","type":"text"}],"id":"b78b6b2a-f01a-4cd0-b8ee-649b0cc90c21","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Use this as your design canvas.","type":"text"}],"id":"5a439f77-ff16-4264-9253-fc36550d02b1","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Public Dataset / Simulated Source Systems\n        ↓\nIngestion Layer\n        ↓\nBronze Layer: Raw Data\n        ↓\nValidation + Quarantine Layer\n        ↓\nSilver Layer: Cleaned and Standardized Data\n        ↓\nTransformation / Modeling Layer\n        ↓\nGold Layer: Fact and Dimension Tables\n        ↓\nAnalytics Layer: KPI Tables + SQL Queries\n        ↓\nDashboard / Repor