ad time, supplier category","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Useful once supplier logic is strong","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"supplier concentration, supplier-driven issues","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Future","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"dim_delivery_route","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Detailed logistics context","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"route, carrier, lane, service level","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Only add if you model route-level data credibly","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"route delays, carrier comparison","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Future","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"184c3dab-e953-43df-8a22-ff835875b72c","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Recommended version-one model:\n","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"fact_order_items","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"fact_deliveries","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"dim_date","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"dim_customer","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"dim_product","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"dim_warehouse","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"dim_region","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":".\nIf time remains, add ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"fact_inventory_snapshot","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". If not, keep inventory as a silver table or a simple Gold KPI mart instead of forcing it into the first star schema.","type":"text"}],"id":"6e1d1bc7-1fe8-4a15-bff9-42f32fdcd86a","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision I need to make:\nWhat should my first version star schema include?\n\nRecommended version 1 model:\nfact_order_items, fact_deliveries, dim_date, dim_customer, dim_product, dim_warehouse, dim_region\n\nOptional future tables:\nfact_inventory_snapshot, dim_supplier, fact_customer_activity, dim_delivery_route\n\nMost important grain decision:\nfact_order_items at one row per order line\n\nInterview defense question:\nWhat is the grain of your fact table and why?\n\nMy final choice:\n[leave blank for me]","type":"text"}],"id":"3f8903e0-74f7-4e67-9066-6957b2adc774","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Design-defense notes","type":"text"}],"id":"f39d6634-993d-4bf1-84ab-98365d82a568","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Use notes like these in ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"docs/design_decisions.md","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":".","type":"text"}],"id":"c8722b12-aa32-4af1-abac-f50088d548c6","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nChoose a Sysco-inspired foodservice distribution analytics theme\n\nWhy this exists:\nPublic Sysco sources center the business on foodservice customers, warehousing, delivery, and digital ordering.\n\nAlternative:\nBuild a generic e-commerce warehouse\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nIt would be easier, but weaker and less targeted for Sysco LABS.\n\nTrade-off:\nThe project becomes more domain-specific, so I must be careful about assumptions.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI wanted a business problem that clearly maps to Sysco’s public operating model instead of a tutorial dataset with a renamed title.","type":"text"}],"id":"cba564de-d138-4316-bc47-cb6f5ff61b40","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nUse Instacart as the core public dataset and simulate missing source systems\n\nWhy this exists:\nIt gives me a strong food/grocery order backbone and lets me model realistic source separation.\n\nAlternative:\nUse one denormalized logistics dataset with everything already present\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nThose datasets usually fit delivery better than foodservice domain relevance.\n\nTrade-off:\nI gain domain fit but must clearly disclose what I simulated.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI prioritized business fit and source-system thinking over convenience.","type":"text"}],"id":"8c73d664-f020-4435-a949-0a121a1e71d5","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nAdd a separate price_book source instead of hiding prices in transformations\n\nWhy this exists:\nPricing is often a separate master or reference source in real systems.\n\nAlternative:\nHardcode random prices directly into the fact table generation\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nThat blurs lineage and makes the design less realistic.\n\nTrade-off:\nIt adds one more table, but improves explainability and lineage.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI wanted missing pricing to become a data-integration problem, not a hidden shortcut.","type":"text"}],"id":"56431c92-5168-4e3e-80b7-117a61878cd9","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nUse deterministic source simulation rather than purely random fake data\n\nWhy this exists:\nDeterministic rules make reruns reproducible and tests reliable.\n\nAlternative:\nGenerate everything randomly with Faker or ad hoc scripts\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nRandom generation is harder to validate and harder to defend in interviews.\n\nTrade-off:\nThe simulated data is less “creative,” but much easier to explain.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI optimized for reproducibility, not randomness.","type":"text"}],"id":"7ddfb2e2-f8eb-4743-906b-801067eabc82","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nUse Bronze, Silver, and Gold layers\n\nWhy this exists:\nThe separation makes lineage, cleaning, and analytics modeling easier to reason about.\n\nAlternative:\nPerform all transformations in one script into one final table\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nIt hides errors, weakens traceability, and makes reruns harder to explain.\n\nTrade-off:\nMore folders and steps, but much better clarity.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI wanted clear separation between raw preservation, source cleaning, and business modeling.","type":"text"}],"id":"54fa8ad1-675d-4c40-b1f1-71adc19a42e6","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nKeep a quarantine layer\n\nWhy this exists:\nI want invalid or suspicious records to be visible and reviewable.\n\nAlternative:\nDrop bad rows silently or fail the whole pipeline every time\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nSilent drops hurt trust, while always failing is too brittle for a realistic reporting pipeline.\n\nTrade-off:\nSlightly more complexity, much better data stewardship.\n\nInterview explanation:\nQuarantine lets me preserve bad data for review without polluting clean reporting tables.","type":"text"}],"id":"b419db37-c9f3-48b0-a520-ec7ede9c52e0","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nUse PySpark and Parquet for the transformation layers\n\nWhy this exists:\nPublic Sysco LABS junior data-engineering roles emphasize Spark-style large-data processing, ETL/ELT, and cloud-style storage patterns.\n\nAlternative:\nUse Pandas for everything\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nPandas would be simpler, but it signals less data-engineering depth for my flagship project.\n\nTrade-off:\nSlightly more setup in exchange for stronger DE signaling.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI chose a toolset that reflects modern pipeline patterns while still being buildable locally.","type":"text"}],"id":"e1ebf5a3-0bc1-4c44-9ef7-bef7ee52e5b0","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nUse a small local warehouse/query engine instead of full cloud deployment\n\nWhy this exists:\nThe interview value comes from data design, quality, SQL, and rerun safety more than cloud infrastructure setup.\n\nAlternative:\nDeploy a full AWS or Azure stack for the portfolio project\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nIt would take much more time and increase the risk of shallow understanding.\n\nTrade-off:\nLess cloud spectacle, stronger explainability.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI kept the build local and portable, then documented how the same design maps to enterprise cloud equivalents.","type":"text"}],"id":"94608089-6725-4b6f-ab3a-cf98df66f934","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nPick fact_order_items as the core fact\n\nWhy this exists:\nOrder-line grain supports the widest range of KPIs without losing flexibility.\n\nAlternative:\nUse fact_orders only\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nOrder-level grain hides product-level behavior and weakens category and SKU analysis.\n\nTrade-off:\nMore rows and more joins, but better analytical power.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI modeled at the lowest grain needed for the KPIs I wanted to answer.","type":"text"}],"id":"5887bcf8-7888-4686-a4e5-8142d96924d0","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nDo a full refresh of Silver and Gold in version one\n\nWhy this exists:\nIt is simpler and safer to explain than premature merge logic.\n\nAlternative:\nStart with complex upserts and partition-level incremental logic\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nThat adds complexity before I have a stable model and stable rules.\n\nTrade-off:\nLess efficiency, more reliability and clarity.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI optimized first for correct, repeatable behavior; then I documented incremental loading as a future improvement.","type":"text"}],"id":"4c699002-1e26-4277-9762-227b441d0dd6","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision:\nDo not overbuild with Airflow, Kafka, Kubernetes, and everything else\n\nWhy this exists:\nA junior flagship project should show depth in a few strong areas.\n\nAlternative:\nAdd many enterprise tools for resume optics\n\nWhy I did not choose the alternative:\nToo many tools make the project harder to finish and harder to defend.\n\nTrade-off:\nA smaller stack, but a stronger story.\n\nInterview explanation:\nI intentionally chose a stack I could fully explain end to end.","type":"text"}],"id":"1cd3601c-e620-4895-acc2-b43a881f3c65","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Pipeline modules","type":"text"}],"id":"c0706aa0-8345-4204-ac6d-4315f075b36e","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":{"columnWidths":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"headerRows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Module","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Purpose","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Input","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Output","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Tools","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Key logic","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Data quality checks","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Idempotency approach","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Definition of done","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Interview talking point","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Dataset acquisition and source simulation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Turn open data into source-style inputs","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Public dataset","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Source-aligned raw extracts","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Python","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Split tables, derive masters, generate deterministic refs","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Source row counts, reproducible seeds","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Regenerate from config and seed","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"You can recreate raw sources from scratch","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"“I made missing systems explicit and reproducible.”","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Ingestion to Bronze","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Land raw data unchanged","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Source extracts","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bronze data + manifest","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Python/PySpark","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Copy and register source files","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"File existence, checksum, schema snapshot","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Append-only by run","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bronze folders populated with audit info","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"“Bronze preserves lineage.”","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Data validation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Test source trustworthiness","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bronze tables","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Validation results","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"PySpark/SQL","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Run rule checks and summarise failures","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"PK, FK, duplicates, bad dates, negatives","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Same rules each run","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"DQ summary table created","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"“I treated validation as a pipeline stage, not an afterthought.”","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Quarantine handling","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Separate bad records","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Validation output","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Quarantine tables and issue logs","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Python/PySpark","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Route invalid rows by rule","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Same as above plus issue severity","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Write by run and issue code","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bad rows retrievable and documented","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"“I avoid silent data loss.”","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Cleaning and standardization","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Apply safe fixes","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Bronze pass records","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Clean standardized records","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"PySpark","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Trim text, cast types, standardize categories and regions","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Type correctness, standardized values","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Rebuilt each run","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Clean tables ready","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"“Silver is source-aligned but usable.”","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Silver layer creation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Create stable cleaned source tables","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Standardized data","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"silver_*","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" tables","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"PySpark/SQL","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Persist cleaned sources separately","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Uniqueness, referential integrity","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Overwrite for v1","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Each source has a clean table","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"“I keep source-cleaning separate from business modeling.”","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Dimensional modeling","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Build conformed model","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Silver tables","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Facts and dimensions","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"SQL/PySpark","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Surrogate keys, conformed dimensions, grain enforcement","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Null FK checks, reconciliation","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Replace target tables on success","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Gold star schema created","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"“The model is designed around reporting questions.”","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Gold KPI marts","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Build stakeholder-ready metrics","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Gold facts and dims","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"KPI tables","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan"