lidation very visible, so this is a strong interview position. citeturn25view0","type":"text"}],"id":"c4cee2ed-2f5e-46f1-a053-7defd540f9af","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision I need to make:\nHow strict should my data validation be?\n\nOptions:\n1. Reject invalid records\n2. Quarantine invalid records\n3. Correct safe issues and flag uncertain issues\n4. Allow records but log warnings\n\nRecommended approach:\n3, with quarantine for critical integrity violations\n\nWhy it is recommended:\nIt is the most realistic balance. Safe formatting issues can be standardized, but broken keys, impossible dates, and invalid quantities should not flow into reporting tables.\n\nInterview defense question:\nHow did you handle bad data?\n\nMy final choice:\n[leave blank for me]","type":"text"}],"id":"8d700858-4715-49bc-b4e4-a055187e8e55","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Idempotency and reruns","type":"text"}],"id":"5e77d5a5-aa96-4d35-b0ab-06c1bced3f81","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"For a junior flagship project, the cleanest version-one rerun strategy is:","type":"text"}],"id":"e5188a51-e7b6-4ec0-ac5c-097c987b5d82","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Bronze:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" append-only by ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"run_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", with a file manifest, checksum, and source metadata.","type":"text"}],"id":"3ecdd85a-c9f7-4845-b49b-594d720c1dc4","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Silver:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" full refresh on each successful run.","type":"text"}],"id":"fbcb3ea2-06a9-4b9b-bb29-a3fe2a347f80","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Gold:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" full refresh on each successful run, ideally using temporary targets and replace-on-success logic.","type":"text"}],"id":"feb0b037-0f31-4ca5-a159-0800382ecc3b","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Quarantine:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" append by ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"run_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":".","type":"text"}],"id":"b4b36bb0-cd2b-4aa7-88d8-640fee1f6329","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Run logging:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" one ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"pipeline_runs","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" table or CSV capturing status, row counts, and timestamps.","type":"text"}],"id":"6ed3bb9e-caf8-4839-8e27-afa27b9bc9a1","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"That means if the pipeline is run twice with the same inputs, Bronze retains immutable raw copies and metadata for both runs, while Silver and Gold are rebuilt cleanly without duplicated reporting rows. If validation fails, the run is recorded as failed or partially failed, invalid rows remain in quarantine, and clean downstream tables are not silently polluted. If Gold creation fails after Silver succeeds, Silver can remain intact and Gold can be safely rerun. This is much easier to explain than jumping straight into complicated merges.","type":"text"}],"id":"e8263d73-70e9-4acd-b446-5b6a4270160c","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":{"columnWidths":[null,null,null,null],"headerRows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Option","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Description","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Best use","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Version-one fit","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Full refresh","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Rebuild Silver and Gold each run","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Small-medium local portfolio projects","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Recommended","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Partition overwrite","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Replace only affected date partitions","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Larger historical loads with stable partitions","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Good future improvement","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Upsert or merge","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Insert/update by natural keys","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Source systems with true incremental feeds","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Future improvement once the model is stable","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]}],"type":"tableContent"},"id":"e738cb57-d71e-41ef-a44e-8c6d8f6f289d","props":{"textColor":"default"},"type":"table"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Decision I need to make:\nWhat rerun/idempotency strategy should I use?\n\nOptions:\n1. Full refresh\n2. Partition overwrite\n3. Upsert/Merge\n\nRecommended approach for version 1:\nFull refresh for Silver and Gold, append-only Bronze and Quarantine\n\nWhy it is recommended:\nIt is the safest, simplest, and most explainable approach for a junior portfolio project.\n\nFuture production improvement:\nPartition overwrite by order date or merge-based incremental loads\n\nInterview defense question:\nHow do you make the pipeline safe to rerun?\n\nMy final choice:\n[leave blank for me]","type":"text"}],"id":"fa5fbdcc-6970-4c71-b37c-2b9d297dc84f","props":{"language":"python"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"KPIs and analytics queries","type":"text"}],"id":"4373e0f5-af4c-4006-8929-9c6cd8913ffe","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":{"columnWidths":[null,null,null,null,null],"headerRows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"KPI","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Business meaning","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Tables needed","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"SQL logic idea","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"},{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Dashboard use","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"tableCell"}]},{"cells":[{"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Total revenue","type":"text"}],"props":{"backgroundColor":"default","colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type"