],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"One-Line Pitch","type":"text"}],"id":"685773ee-df5e-4187-88b7-27be52770f55","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":4,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"A production-minded data engineering project that simulates how a foodservice distributor could move order, product, customer, pricing, warehouse, and delivery data from source-style inputs into a Bronze/Silver/Gold analytics platform.","type":"text"}],"id":"210430be-9aa5-4722-82f9-4a1457f2aad5","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Business Scenario","type":"text"}],"id":"01c040f4-63cc-434d-a24e-6083bc2c3a55","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":4,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"A foodservice distributor needs a reliable analytics layer to unify order, product, customer, pricing, warehouse, and delivery data so operations and business teams can track category revenue, account activity, fulfillment performance, and emerging stock or service risks.","type":"text"}],"id":"f3e9d37a-1acc-438d-b4b7-2df0578f37d1","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Why This Targets Sysco LABS","type":"text"}],"id":"ab23ae7e-d13c-46c7-8051-8f0964b8a5f9","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":4,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Public Sysco sources emphasize away-from-home foodservice customers, warehousing, daily delivery, digital ordering, and inventory-related support. Public Sysco LABS material says its technology footprint spans sourcing, merchandising, warehouse operation