the specific JOIN type, and you missed a small instruction from the prompt.","type":"text"}],"id":"5d91a7be-6db9-4f43-9734-886bd22634e5","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"The Intent:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" The question explicitly asks for a report ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"only where a matching account actually exists","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". The correct textbook SQL approach for returning records only when there is a match in ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"both","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" tables is an ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"INNER JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":".","type":"text"}],"id":"c745da0d-e889-43b5-9768-657c4a075d66","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Why RIGHT JOIN isn''t the best fit:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" While your ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"RIGHT JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" will actually produce the correct output against this specific seed data (because the foreign key constraint ensures no account can exist without a valid customer), semantically, a ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"RIGHT JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" means \"return all accounts, even if they don''t have a matching customer.\" Using an ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"INNER JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" directly answers the strict \"only where matches exist\" criteria.","type":"text"}],"id":"df2022c8-f93a-4ac5-a6da-8b4269110ebf","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Missing Requirement:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" The question also asked you to specifically ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"name the JOIN type used","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". In an interview, make sure to explicitly state: \"The join type used is an INNER JOIN.\"","type":"text"}],"id":"85ad7204-c97a-4014-a08d-511bcee363c7","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Corrected / Optimized Query:","type":"text"}],"id":"9575902b-682f-4907-ba45-89c57ad4d08b","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"SELECT c.customer_id, c.name, a.account_id, a.account_type\nFROM customers AS c\nINNER JOIN accounts AS a \n    ON c.customer_id = a.customer_id;\n","type":"text"}],"id":"5e330473-5bab-4c99-b50e-caa9ab99ab8a","props":{"language":"sql"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":"(Note: Writing just ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" is perfectly fine too, as it defaults to ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"INNER JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{"italic":true},"text":" in both PostgreSQL and MySQL).","type":"text"}],"id":"2a2f2b84-49db-4758-8503-e553ceb8f5f3","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Expected Output (Mental Trace):","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Running this query successfully excludes customers ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C4","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C6","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C8","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", as they have no entries in the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"accounts","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" table. The result set will contain exactly 10 rows, corresponding directly to the 10 accounts mapped to their respective owners.","type":"text"}],"id":"5b2d672d-e2b9-4f68-a607-390fcd6ad1f7","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[],"id":"2711e506-c949-4eb4-9751-a6a697ae6156","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Using this dataset, write a query to list ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"every customer","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", including those with no accounts (e.g., C4, C6, C8), showing NULLs for account columns where missing.","type":"text"}],"id":"177ba402-4ee3-44c1-a559-384f1379de6b","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","start":2,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"numberedListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[],"id":"7993178a-0724-4e75-a6f7-d1d9f9d570c0","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Question 2 Evaluation","type":"text"}],"id":"fd8bb522-7e6d-4ca2-a76d-618891d42145","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Your Answer:","type":"text"}],"id":"fcd26e34-9e2a-4575-81b0-93b15bc1738e","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"SELECT c.customer_id, c.name , a.account_id, a.account_type\nFROM customers AS c\nLEFT JOIN accounts as a ON c.customer_id = a.customer_id\n","type":"text"}],"id":"54c3f1cd-2abc-4229-8409-dbb248ee0a7b","props":{"language":"sql"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"id":"b2591fe8-fcc8-4461-b0fe-1571e48bf408","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Feedback","type":"text"}],"id":"145e5dd9-ae47-4721-abd8-8d4319ea8af6","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Spot on!","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" 🎯","type":"text"}],"id":"8064508a-b10a-4211-bc94-a1eee3836472","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"This query is completely correct. By placing ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"customers","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" on the left and using a ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"LEFT JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"LEFT OUTER JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":"), you ensure that every single customer record is retained regardless of whether they have a matching account in the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"accounts","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" table.","type":"text"}],"id":"29c077e9-3470-47f7-a58d-e68ddbfb2687","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Logic:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" For customers without matching accounts, PostgreSQL/MySQL will automatically fill the account-related columns (","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"a.account_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"a.account_type","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":") with ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"NULL","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":"s.","type":"text"}],"id":"976dc974-201c-46c8-8a9a-3fdafcf186b6","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Best Practice:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Using clear alias names (","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"c","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"a","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":") makes the query concise and readable.","type":"text"}],"id":"bc0d74fd-de27-4b1c-86ae-59a9754a3aee","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"id":"f4faad89-1ad6-4611-87d1-b80f1446917c","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Expected Output (Mental Trace)","type":"text"}],"id":"cc5d677b-abea-49d1-a489-bd9b9cb04efd","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Since the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"customers","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" table has 8 rows and 3 of them (","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C4","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C6","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C8","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":") have no accounts, the result set will contain ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"13 rows total","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":":","type":"text"}],"id":"cdaa1b32-f860-4ac9-9915-d9d6bb26fdfe","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"10 rows","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" for customers who have matching accounts (e.g., ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C1","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" appears 3 times, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C5","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" twice, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C7","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" twice, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C2","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" twice, ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C3","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" once).","type":"text"}],"id":"7950f55d-7a52-4bdb-aba9-8340def23616","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"3 rows","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C4","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C6","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"C8","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":", where ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"account_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"account_type","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" display as ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"NULL","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":".","type":"text"}],"id":"eaa23b36-7df3-4328-bc64-9e4143d527a3","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Ready for ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Question 3","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" whenever you are!","type":"text"}],"id":"9d209cc2-c2d4-48e8-919e-9ed8edeb8245","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[],"id":"d6bdfc5c-9085-41be-924e-9d1fa34a0d1f","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"EY''s compliance team wants a list of ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"customers who have never opened an account","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":". Using the \"NULL trick\" on a LEFT JOIN, write the query. Which customers should appear in the result?","type":"text"}],"id":"84fb97bd-8a3f-43fd-ae5c-5064c673ee76","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"numberedListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Question 3 Evaluation","type":"text"}],"id":"cfb9081c-bf3f-425a-b700-0f7105dca2fc","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Your Answer:","type":"text"}],"id":"f0467f3b-6f7b-4a98-be11-e7ccddf1d16c","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"SELECT c.customer_id, c.name , a.account_id, a.account_type\nFROM customers AS c\nLEFT JOIN accounts as a ON c.customer_id = a.customer_id\nWHERE a.account_id IS NULL\n","type":"text"}],"id":"6e69ac6d-1a8a-4347-a994-7a288c130bba","props":{"language":"sql"},"type":"codeBlock"},{"children":[],"id":"505c4565-3c79-43f9-a6f0-9120648e5eea","props":{},"type":"divider"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"Feedback","type":"text"}],"id":"6c684910-8584-4852-9590-b20c39fb11f7","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","isToggleable":false,"level":3,"textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"heading"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Excellent work!","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" 🎯","type":"text"}],"id":"96176e9b-6a6b-4c72-87e0-1c8ea4f3107d","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{},"text":"This is the textbook implementation of the ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"\"NULL trick\"","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" (a anti-join pattern).","type":"text"}],"id":"74b9f6f6-bf0b-4765-a386-4e8e1d4f96eb","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"paragraph"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Logic:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" By performing a ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"LEFT JOIN","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" and then filtering with ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"WHERE a.account_id IS NULL","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"WHERE a.customer_id IS NULL","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":"), you filter out all matching records, leaving only the rows from the left table (","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"customers","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":") that have no corresponding records in the right table (","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"accounts","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":").","type":"text"}],"id":"75972bd6-eabc-469b-b41c-779a47ccc542","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"default"},"type":"bulletListItem"},{"children":[],"content":[{"styles":{"bold":true},"text":"Optimization Note:","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" Checking ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"a.account_id IS NULL","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" is ideal because ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"account_id","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" is the Primary Key of ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"accounts","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":" and is guaranteed never to be naturally ","type":"text"},{"styles":{"code":true},"text":"NULL","type":"text"},{"styles":{},"text":".","type":"text"}],"id":"6c49533b-5a05-4d60-a92b-db7e78f7105a","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","textColor":"defaul