Hey, I just wrapped up a 1-hour architecture planning meeting from 9:00 to 10:00 AM about our client-facing AI prototypes.

Basically, more and more clients are asking us to integrate AI into their workflows—mainly RAG chat agents over internal manuals and company policies, as well as AI calling agents. We discussed our approach and agreed on a breadth-first strategy: build lightweight, reusable MVP prototypes to demo to clients, but ensure the architecture is expandable so we can go deep and deploy directly to production without a rewrite once a client approves.

Rather than starting from scratch, we decided to use the hierarchical system our Principal Engineer built as our foundation. He gave me access to the codebase. We also evaluated candidate APIs and shortlisted the best choices while ruling out the weaker ones.

Coming out of the meeting, I have two tasks assigned to me for today:

Understand the existing system: review the Principal Engineer’s codebase, the hierarchical architecture, key design decisions, and component implementation.
Identify expansion requirements: audit what the system currently supports, find the gaps, and define what we need to build for RAG and calling agents.

Can you log this meeting to my Work Journal and also add these two action items to my To-Do list for today?"
